CORE
main.c
--refine-concurrency --verbosity 9
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^Refinement 1: added \d+ constraints violated by the model$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ coherent: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ both writes may be seen: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
With --refine-concurrency, the from-read constraints are added as models of
the solver violate them: without them, b could read the first write after a
read the second one.
